arch community\nFacilities and equipment\nOur impact\nResearch outputs\nResearch excellence framework (REF)\nCollaboration: innovation and growth\nOur partners\nInnovation assets and capabilities\nKnowledge Exchange Framework (KEF)\nContact us\nPostgraduate research\nDoctoral Training\nFellowships\nResearch environment\nResearcher support\nResearch news\nOriginal Ideas podcast\nClose\nBack\nGlobal Liverpool\nPartnerships\nStrategic partners\nGlobal networks\nTransnational education partners\nCollaborate with us\nGlobal study opportunities\nStudy abroad\nStudy in Liverpool\nStudy in China\nStudy in India\nAchievements and rankings\nOur global city\nSustainability\nOur global team\nLeadership team\nGlobal contacts\nOur global community\nClose\nBack\nAbout us\nThe University\nOur history\nStrategy and vision\nPeople and culture\nRankings and reputation\nReports, policies and governance documents\nOur structure\nWork at Liverpool\nOur city, our inspiration\nDiscover Liverpool\nOur commitment to the Liverpool City Region\nProfessional Services\nIT Services\nHuman Resources\nLegal\nOur campus\nCampus facilities\nLibraries\nSports facilities\nSustainability\nEquality, diversity and inclusion\nNews\nEvents\nLiverpool Literary Festival\nHire an event space\nVisit us\nMuseums and Collections\nCar parking\nContact us\nNews\nJobs\nDonate\nA-Z\nAlumni\nStaff\nStudents\nSearch the site\nSchool of Engineering\nAlso in this section\nMore\nAbout us\nEquality, diversity and inclusion\nAthena Swan\nDepartments\nStudy\nUndergraduate\nCourses\nCivil Engineering\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering\nPlacements in industry\nYear in industry FAQs\nUndergraduate stories\nLearning, Assessment and Support\nPostgraduate taught\nWhy choose us\nVirtual tour\nResearch\nPartners\nAdvanced Materials Symposium\nFacilities\nDesign Studio\nActive Learning Labs\nFlight simulators\nHELIFLIGHT-R\nHydraulics Lab\nLarge recirculating water channel\nMaterials and Structural Laboratory\nBiomedical Engineering labs\nAdditive Manufacturing labs\nStaff\nNews\nContact us\nLiverpool Women in Science & Engineering\nOutreach\nResources for teachers\nGirls into Electronics\nAlso in this section\nMore\nPartners\nAdvanced Materials Symposium\nhome\nSchool of Engineering\nResearch\nResearch\nWe provide a well-equipped, well-resourced research environment that encourages collaboration across disciplines, departments and organisations.\nResearch is focused on four key themes to reflect today's key challenges:\nCivil and Environmental Engineering\nElectrical Engineering and Electronics\nMaterials, Design and Manufacturing Engineering\nMechanical and Aerospace Engineering.\nThese provide platforms for the School's specialists in fields such as aerospace engineering, civil engineering, mechanical engineering, materials engineering, signal processing, design and manufacturing, robotics and clean and renewable energy.\nCollaborations\nOur programmes frequently involve external partners, both academic and industrial, regionally, nationally and internationally.\nThe Virtual Engineering Centre (VEC) is the leading technology innovation centre for engineering development using Virtual Engineering technologies and expertise. The VEC is a partnership between, the School of Engineering at the University of Liverpool, the Science and Technology Facilities Council (STFC), BAE Systems, North West Aerospace Alliance (NWAA) and Morson Projects.\nChadwick Institute for Nuclear Innovation forms a hub of advanced interdisciplinary nuclear science and technology research.\nLooking ahead\nAs part of an elite Russell Group of universities, we have significant funds to invest in research and are constantly searching for new opportunities.\nWe are keen to speak to potential partners and to expand our community of postgraduate and PhD students in line with our expanding research programme.\nResearch impact\nThe School of Engineering has a dynamic and diverse range of world leading engineering research clusters spanning functional materials, biomaterials and biomechanics, additive manufacturing, transport infrastructure, risk and uncertainty, aerospace and fluid mechanics.\nAcceleration of impact for the research being developed is maintained by engaging key stakeholders and end-users to ensure broadest reach and significance is achieved.\nImproving the management of glaucoma\nOur biomechanical engineering researchers have improved the management of glaucoma, developing more accurate techniques to avoid misdiagnosis and allow optimal treatment of this vision-threatening condition.\nDeveloping advanced additive manufacturing technology\nOur engineering researchers have developed and patented an additive manufacturing technology, improving orthopaedic and spinal implants for patients around the world.\nReducing industrial development times in nuclear and aerospace sectors\nOur structural mechanics researchers have used virtual engineering technology to support industry in reducing development times.\nImproving the treatment of retinal detachment\nA multidisciplinary team of our researchers have developed novel silicone oil tamponades that have improved the surgical treatment of retinal detachments.\nUnlocking manufacturing competitiveness for UK industry\nResearchers in our Virtual Engineering Centre have collaborated with UK industry to unlock manufacturing competitiveness across a range of sectors through the application of cutting-edge digital engineering approaches.\nSupporting UK naval ship design and aircraft operations\nOur aerospace engineering researchers have developed advanced modelling and flight simulation tools for the assessment of ship aerodynamics and its impact on the workload of pilots.\nPostgraduate research\nWithin the School of Engineering we provide a well-equipped, well-resourced research environment that encourages collaboration across disciplines, departments and organisations.\nSection footer\nSchool of Engineering\nPart of the\nFaculty of Science and Engineering.\nUseful links\nStaff intranet\nHealth and Safety in Engineering\nOur address\nSchool of Engineering\nUniversity of Liverpool\nThe Quadrangle\nBrownlow Hill\nLiverpool\nL69 3GH\nUnited Kingdom\nGet in touch\n+44 (0)151 794 4859\nWebsite footer\nInformation for\nCurrent students\nCurrent staff\nProspective students\nBusinesses and partners\nResearchers\nMedia\nStudy at Liverpool\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate taught\nPostgraduate research\nOnline courses\nCPD\nContinuing education\nInternational students\nQuick links\nJobs at Liverpool\nLibrary\nSport at Liverpool\nFind a researcher\nAlumni\nOur departments and faculties\nAll subjects\nContact us\nUniversity of Liverpool\nFoundation Building\nBrownlow Hill\nLiverpool\nL69 7ZX\nTelephone\n+44 (0) 151 794 2000\nContact us\nMaps and directions\nVisit us\nPart of the Russell Group\nAccessibility\nFreedom of information\nCookie information\nData Protection\nModern slavery statement\nTerms and Conditions\nCharitable status\n\u00a9 University of Liverpool", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/engineering/research/#main-content"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/undergraduate/"], ["Postgraduate", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/postgraduate-taught/"], ["PhD", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/study/postgraduate-research/"], ["Accommodation", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/accommodation/"], ["Research", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/research/"], ["International students", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/international/"], ["A-Z index", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/a-z/"], ["UK", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/"], ["China", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/xjtlu/"], ["India", "https://www.bengaluru.liverpool.ac.uk/"], ["Online", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/study/online/"], ["Home", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/"], ["Menu", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/engineering/research/#main-menu"], ["Menu", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk/engineering/research/"], ["Study", "https://www.liverpool.ac.uk